From: Duke Eagleman <301139544+jerricky26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42l42: Stay on the oscillator if the PLL does not lock

cs42l42_mute_stream() only warns when the PLL fails to lock, then
switches MCLK to the PLL and turns off the internal oscillator. With no
SCLK that leaves the codec without any clock: its control port stops
answering and can hold up the I2C bus, which on Apple tablets is shared
with the PMIC.

On a lock failure stop the PLL, keep the oscillator and return the
error.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l42.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l42.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l42.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l42.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l42.c
@@ -1100,8 +1100,19 @@
 							       (regval & 1),
 							       CS42L42_PLL_LOCK_POLL_US,
 							       CS42L42_PLL_LOCK_TIMEOUT_US);
-				if (ret < 0)
-					dev_warn(component->dev, "PLL failed to lock: %d\n", ret);
+				if (ret < 0) {
+					/*
+					 * Without SCLK the PLL never locks. Keep the
+					 * internal oscillator: switching to the PLL
+					 * or marking SCLK present would leave the
+					 * codec without a clock, and its control port
+					 * would then hold up the I2C bus it shares.
+					 */
+					dev_err(component->dev, "PLL failed to lock: %d\n", ret);
+					snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, CS42L42_PLL_CTL1,
+								      CS42L42_PLL_START_MASK, 0);
+					return ret;
+				}
 
 				/* PLL must be running to drive glitchless switch logic */
 				snd_soc_component_update_bits(component,
